.TH CHTTPSVR_REQ_BODY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_req_body \- access the buffered request body
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpserver.h>

const void *chttpsvr_req_body(const chttpsvr_req *req,
                               size_t *len_out);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns a pointer to the buffered request body bytes.  If len_out is
non-NULL, the body length in bytes is stored there.  Returns NULL and
stores 0 if there is no body, or if req belongs to a streaming route
(chttpsvr_register_streaming_handler); a streaming route's body is
never pre-extracted; use chttpsvr_req_read instead.

The buffer is valid for the lifetime of the handler invocation.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_req_read (3)
